            <ArticleTitle>Stent fracture and restenosis after zotarolimus-eluting stent implantation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e29-31</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.ijcard.2009.01.030</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Stent fracture (SF) has been found in peripheral and coronary vasculatures, and in the latter mostly after implantation of sirolimus- or paclitaxel-eluting stents. We report a patient with a fractured stent associated with restenosis after zotarolimus-eluting stent (ZES) implantation which was confirmed by fluoroscopy, intravascular ultrasound and computerized tomography. To our knowledge, this is the first published report of SF after ZES implantation.</AbstractText>
